   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello,<div><br></div><div>I apologize if this comes off as a beginner question, as I am just getting started with <i>mirt </i>and CAT. I ran the <i>mirt </i>function for a simulated 5-item polytomous response pattern using a GPCM model. However, some of the betas for the response options were &quot;NA.&quot; I&#39;ve produced the parameters for the first 10 questions, as reference.</div><div><br></div><div> </div><table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"384\" style=\"text-align:center;border-collapse:collapse;width:288pt\">\r\n <colgroup><col width=\"64\" span=\"6\" style=\"width:48pt\">\r\n </colgroup><tbody><tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" width=\"64\" style=\"height:15.0pt;width:48pt\">id</td>\r\n  <td width=\"64\" style=\"width:48pt\">a</td>\r\n  <td width=\"64\" style=\"width:48pt\">b1</td>\r\n  <td width=\"64\" style=\"width:48pt\">b2</td>\r\n  <td width=\"64\" style=\"width:48pt\">b3</td>\r\n  <td width=\"64\" style=\"width:48pt\">b4</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt;text-align:right\">1</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">2.188891</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">0.799167</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">0.171552</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">-0.4231</td>\r\n  <td>NA</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt;text-align:right\">2</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">3.116017</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">0.289836</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">-0.45773</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">-0.36974</td>\r\n  <td>NA</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt;text-align:right\">3</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">3.363451</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">-0.07045</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">-0.09065</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">0.07369</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">0.040219</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt;text-align:right\">4</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">2.604773</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">-0.28404</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">-0.20778</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">-0.09344</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">0.42448</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt;text-align:right\">5</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">2.307046</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">-0.60988</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">0.165687</td>\r\n  <td>NA</td>\r\n  <td>NA</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt;text-align:right\">6</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">2.477962</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">0.108575</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">0.308608</td>\r\n  <td>-0.03472</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">0.061221</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt;text-align:right\">7</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">3.512669</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">0.101464</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">-0.28706</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">0.436758</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">0.413581</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt;text-align:right\">8</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">3.225537</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">0.283565</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">0.420048</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">0.239907</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">-0.32759</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt;text-align:right\">9</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">2.571879</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">-0.11952</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">-0.49139</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">-0.1683</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">-0.26689</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt;text-align:right\">10</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">2.870999</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">-0.01151</td>\r\n  <td>NA</td>\r\n  <td>NA</td>\r\n  <td>NA</td>\r\n </tr></tbody></table><div><br></div><div>I&#39;ve read a few papers, and some papers produce IRT parameters with no missing values, while others produce IRT parameters with some &quot;NA&quot;s, like mine above. Is there a way to produce a full set of IRT parameters without any missing parameters? Thank you.</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
