  {
   "id": "3L3ixMk4EgAJ",
   "from": "Phil Chalmers",
   "author": "b330c2028fed415b",
   "date": "2019-01-17T15:11:57Z",
   "subject": "Re: \"NA\" values for some beta estimates in polyCAT",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">The NAs are just placholders. E.g., item 1 seems to have 4 response categories observed, while item 3 has 5 response categories observed. If you have categories that were not endorsed then the intercepts/difficult parameters would not be identified for those categories, and in mirt these are structurally ignored. HTH. <div><br clear=\"all\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Phil</div></div></div></div><br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Thu, Jan 17, 2019 at 10:09 AM coreankim &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">core...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello,<div><br></div><div>I apologize if this comes off as a beginner question, as I am just getting started with <i>mirt </i>and CAT. I ran the <i>mirt </i>function for a simulated 5-item polytomous response pattern using a GPCM model. However, some of the betas for the response options were &quot;NA.&quot; I&#39;ve produced the parameters for the first 10 questions, as reference.</div><div><br></div><div> </div><table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"384\" style=\"text-align:center;border-collapse:collapse;width:288pt\">\r\n <colgroup><col width=\"64\" span=\"6\" style=\"width:48pt\">\r\n </colgroup><tbody><tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" width=\"64\" style=\"height:15pt;width:48pt\">id</td>\r\n  <td width=\"64\" style=\"width:48pt\">a</td>\r\n  <td width=\"64\" style=\"width:48pt\">b1</td>\r\n  <td width=\"64\" style=\"width:48pt\">b2</td>\r\n  <td width=\"64\" style=\"width:48pt\">b3</td>\r\n  <td width=\"64\" style=\"width:48pt\">b4</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt;text-align:right\">1</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">2.188891</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">0.799167</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">0.171552</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">-0.4231</td>\r\n  <td>NA</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt;text-align:right\">2</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">3.116017</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">0.289836</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">-0.45773</td>\r\n  <td style=\"text-align:right\">-0.36974</td>\r\n  <td>NA</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15pt;text-align:right\">3</td>\r\n  <td